title: The Entity menu, laid out
intro: What you can add is sorted into categories, each thing with an icon and a line saying what it makes, and Add Entity finds it as you type.
project: Platformer | Entity Menu

chapter: Categories | Entity > Characters > Grid Enemy
say: The Entity menu used to be one long list. Now it's sorted into categories: basics, characters, gameplay, the level, physics, UI, story, audio, lights and effects, and genres, with one for each genre module, so the menu stays short however many there are.
deselect
menu: Entity > Characters > Grid Enemy
expectselected: Enemy
explain: component:GridChase | Grid Enemy | Every item has an icon, and hovering it says what it makes. This one is an enemy that chases the player tile by tile.

chapter: Add Entity | Type to find it
deselect
entitylist
explain: entitylist | Add Entity | The plus at the top of the Hierarchy, or Control Shift A, opens Add Entity: everything the menu makes, by category, each with a line saying what it is.
explain: entitylist:recent:Grid Enemy | Recent | What you made lately is at the top, so the enemy from a moment ago is one key away. It's remembered between sessions.
type: waterfall
explain: entitylist:list | Found by what it does | Typing searches names, categories and what things do. A waterfall finds the sound source, a sound that loops where it's put.
explain: entitylist:plan | What Enter makes | Underneath, it says what Enter will make.
key: Enter
expectselected: Sound Source
explain: component:SoundSource | Sound Source | Audio is a category of its own now, with music, looping sounds, sounds that play on a message, and a beat clock.

chapter: Right-click the Hierarchy | The same categories
hierarchymenu: Lights and Effects > Light
expectselected: Light
explain: entity:Light | Same place, every time | Right-clicking the Hierarchy has the same categories, so things to add are where you expect them wherever you start.
say: The menu items are the same commands as before, so agents' tools didn't change, and each one says its category to them too.
